 ### [DoF-NeRF](9432-dof-nerf.md)
-DoF-NeRF is a neural rendering framework that extends the standard Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) architecture to simulate the depth-of-field (DoF) effects of a physical lens, allowing it to operate on and synthesize views with arbitrary focus configurations. Unlike standard NeRF or methods like RawNeRF and NeRFocus which assume all-in-focus inputs, DoF-NeRF explicitly models the aperture and focus distance, enabling the optimization of a clear, all-in-focus 3D scene representation from shallow DoF inputs. It achieves this by combining optical models with volume rendering to compute observed colors based on the Circle of Confusion (CoC) diameter. Choose this method when training on images with shallow depth-of-field and the goal is to recover a sharp, all-in-focus 3D representation.
