 ### [MINE](13661-mine.md)
-MINE is a novel view synthesis method that models the frustum of the source camera using a continuous depth Multiplane Image (MPI) representation, conditioned on input images via a fully-convolutional decoder. Unlike pixelNeRF and GRF, which model the entire 3D space per ray, MINE reconstructs the frustum of the source camera per plane, allowing rendering of any target view via homography warping after a single encoder pass and a fixed number of decoder passes, independent of the number of target views. This architectural choice makes MINE significantly more efficient than ray-based methods when rendering multiple novel views. Choose this method for efficient multi-view synthesis from a single or few source views.
