 ## Background
-The original implementation by Mildenhall et al. [1] employed hierarchical rendering to improve computational efficiency, using two networks (coarse and fine) to guide sampling point selection [S1]. Subsequent works have focused on accelerating training and inference, improving geometry, and extending NeRF to new domains such as dynamic scenes, human avatars, and generalizable synthesis. The field has evolved from simple MLP-based density fields to complex architectures incorporating transformers, SDFs, voxel grids, and physics-based simulations.
